note S5 scrub, then a write and a read of a short global (length 100: a base pin only, its length check is
note an immediate) declared after the scrubbing function. omc 0d7f2f42 pinned its base and the scrub left
note it 0, so the put stored to an unmapped low address (SIGSEGV, exit 139) instead of the global. Exit 0 is
note the pass.
om2
fn clean to ulong
k = scrub 64
ret ulong k
end
global s ulong 100
fn main to int
j = ulong 10
k = clean
put s j 9
y = get s j
if ne y 9
ret 2
end
ret int k
end
